# Database

- PostgreSQL is the source of truth; core business objects cannot live only in
  component state.
- Represent every schema or policy change in a version-controlled Supabase
  migration. Never edit production schema manually.
- Regenerate and commit strict TypeScript database types after schema changes.
- Model roles through school memberships, club memberships, and assignments;
  never hard-code role ownership into application records.
- Use foreign keys, constraints, tenant identifiers, and transactions to preserve
  integrity. Add indexes for tenant filters and common query paths.
- Keep audit events append-oriented and omit secrets, email bodies, and unnecessary
  PII from metadata.
- Store file metadata only; file binaries belong in Storage.
